msgid "Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:179
msgid ""
"Copy and paste the complete code into the ``launch/example_main_launch.py`` "
"file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:181
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch.actions import IncludeLaunchDescription\n"
"from launch.substitutions import PathJoinSubstitution\n"
"from launch_ros.substitutions import FindPackageShare\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    colors = {\n"
"        'background_r': '200'\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        IncludeLaunchDescription(\n"
"            PathJoinSubstitution([\n"
"                FindPackageShare('launch_tutorial'),\n"
"                'launch',\n"
"                'example_substitutions_launch.py'\n"
"            ]),\n"
"            launch_arguments={\n"
"                'turtlesim_ns': 'turtlesim2',\n"
"                'use_provided_red': 'True',\n"
"                'new_background_r': colors['background_r'],\n"
"            }.items()\n"
"        )\n"
"    ])\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:184
msgid ""
"The ``FindPackageShare`` substitution is used to find the path to the "
"``launch_tutorial`` package. The ``PathJoinSubstitution`` substitution is "
"then used to join the path to that package path with the "
"``example_substitutions_launch.py`` file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:187
msgid ""
"            PathJoinSubstitution([\n"
"                FindPackageShare('launch_tutorial'),\n"
"                'launch',\n"
"                'example_substitutions_launch.py'\n"
"            ]),\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:193
msgid ""
"A list of substitutions or strings gets concatenated into a single string. "
"This generally applies to anything that supports substitutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:196
msgid ""
"For example, with ``PathJoinSubstitution``, if the file name prefix depended "
"on a launch argument named ``file``, a list of substitutions and strings "
"could be used to create the file name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:198
msgid ""
"# Make sure to import LaunchConfiguration:\n"
"# from launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration\n"
"\n"
"PathJoinSubstitution([\n"
"    FindPackageShare('launch_tutorial'),\n"
"    'launch',\n"
"    [LaunchConfiguration('file', default='example_substitutions'), "
"'_launch', '.py']\n"
"])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:209
msgid ""
"In this case, by default, the last path component provided to "
"``PathJoinSubstitution`` would resolve to ``example_substitutions_launch."
"py`` and would then be joined with the other path components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:211
msgid ""
"The ``launch_arguments`` dictionary with ``turtlesim_ns`` and "
"``use_provided_red`` arguments is passed to the ``IncludeLaunchDescription`` "
