#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:219
msgid "3 Substitutions example launch file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:221
msgid "Now create the substitution launch file in the same folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:227
msgid ""
"Create the file ``launch/example_substitutions_launch.xml`` and insert the "
"following code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:229
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"<launch>\n"
"  <arg name=\"turtlesim_ns\" default=\"turtlesim1\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"use_provided_red\" default=\"False\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"new_background_r\" default=\"200\" />\n"
"\n"
"  <node pkg=\"turtlesim\" namespace=\"$(var turtlesim_ns)\" "
"exec=\"turtlesim_node\" name=\"sim\" />\n"
"  <executable cmd=\"ros2 service call $(var turtlesim_ns)/spawn "
"turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn '{x: 5, y: 2, theta: 0.2}'\" />\n"
"  <executable cmd=\"ros2 param set $(var turtlesim_ns)/sim background_r "
"120\" />\n"
"  <timer period=\"2.0\">\n"
"    <executable cmd=\"ros2 param set $(var turtlesim_ns)/sim background_r "
"$(var new_background_r)\"\n"
"      if=\"$(eval '$(var new_background_r) == 200 and $(var "
"use_provided_red)')\" />\n"
"  </timer>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:232
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:272
msgid ""
"The ``turtlesim_ns``, ``use_provided_red``, and ``new_background_r`` launch "
"configurations are defined. They are used to store values of launch "
"arguments in the above variables and to pass them to required actions. The "
"launch configuration arguments can later be used with the ``$(var <name>)`` "
"substitution to acquire the value of the launch argument in any part of the "
"launch description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:236
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:276
msgid ""
"The ``arg`` tag is used to define the launch argument that can be passed "
"from the above launch file or from the console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:238
msgid ""
"  <arg name=\"turtlesim_ns\" default=\"turtlesim1\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"use_provided_red\" default=\"False\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"new_background_r\" default=\"200\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:242
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:282
msgid ""
"The ``turtlesim_node`` node with the ``namespace`` set to the "
"``turtlesim_ns`` launch configuration value using the ``$(var <name>)`` "
"substitution is defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:244
msgid ""
"  <node pkg=\"turtlesim\" namespace=\"$(var turtlesim_ns)\" "
"exec=\"turtlesim_node\" name=\"sim\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:248
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:288
msgid ""
"Afterwards, an ``executable`` action is defined with the corresponding "
"``cmd`` tag. This command makes a call to the spawn service of the turtlesim "
"node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:251
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:291
msgid ""
"Additionally, the ``$(var <name>)`` substitution is used to get the value of "
"the ``turtlesim_ns`` launch argument to construct a command string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:253
msgid ""
"  <executable cmd=\"ros2 service call $(var turtlesim_ns)/spawn "
"turtlesim_msgs/srv/Spawn '{x: 5, y: 2, theta: 0.2}'\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:257
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:297
msgid ""
"The same approach is used for the ``ros2 param`` ``executable`` actions that "
"change the turtlesim background's red color parameter. The difference is "
"that the second action inside of the timer is only executed if the provided "
"``new_background_r`` argument equals ``200`` and the ``use_provided_red`` "
"launch argument is set to ``True``. The evaluation of the ``if`` predicate "
"is done using the ``$(eval <python-expression>)`` substitution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Launch/Using-Substitutions.rst:261
msgid ""
"  <executable cmd=\"ros2 param set $(var turtlesim_ns)/sim background_r "
"120\" />\n"
"  <timer period=\"2.0\">\n"
"    <executable cmd=\"ros2 param set $(var turtlesim_ns)/sim background_r "
"$(var new_background_r)\"\n"
"      if=\"$(eval '$(var new_background_r) == 200 and $(var "
"use_provided_red)')\" />\n"
"  </timer>\n"
msgstr ""

